This patch is maintained against containerd v2.2.5-k3s2. Apply the following
changes to `pkg/sys/unshare_linux.go` when containerd runs inside a nested
Sysbox user namespace:

```diff
@@ UnshareAfterEnterUserns
-            Ptrace:    true,
+            // Sysbox's seccomp filter rejects PTRACE_TRACEME in L1. The
+            // pidfd below provides the required lifetime synchronization.
+            Ptrace:    false,
@@ parseIDMapping, after validating IDs
+    if normalized, ok := normalizeHostID(hID); ok {
+        hID = normalized
+    }
```

Add `normalizeHostID` to parse `/proc/self/uid_map` and map a HostID outside
the caller's container-ID ranges (for example kubelet's L0 `231072`) to local
root `0`. The same normalization must be applied to GID mappings and to
`WithRemapperLabels` in `internal/cri/server/helpers_linux.go` and
`podsandbox/helpers_linux.go`; otherwise overlay snapshot ownership can still
fail with EINVAL. This source-level patch has not yet been built into the
K3s-embedded containerd; do not claim L2 `hostUsers:false` support until the
patched binary is selected through `--container-runtime-endpoint` and the
sandbox regression passes.
